        <body>
            <div xml:id="d391-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0552" n="510" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg510"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate, Nassau</hi>,
                            N. P.</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-01-26"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">January</hi> 26,
                    1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to inform you of the
                    arrival at this port, this morning, of the confederate steamer Florida, late the
                    noted Oreto, Maffit, late of the United States navy, commander.</p>
                <p>This pirate ship entered this port without any restrictions, with the secession
                    flag <hi rendition="#italic">at her peak</hi>, and the secession war pennant <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at the main</hi>, and anchored abreast of her Britannic
                    Majesty’s steamer Barracouta, Maffit and his officers landing in the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">garrison boat</hi>, escorted by the port-adjutant,
                    Williams, of the 2d W. I. regiment.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>The privateer soon after anchoring commenced coaling, by permission of the
                    authorities—an evidence of the perfect neutrality which exists here, where the
                    United States steamer Dacotah, but a few months since, was only permitted to
                    take on board twenty tons of coal from an American bark, off Hog island; and
                    only then, on Captain McHinstry and myself pledging ourselves, in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">writing</hi>, that within ten days after leaving this
                    port she would not be cruising <hi rendition="#italic">within five miles</hi> of
                        <hi rendition="#italic">any island</hi> of the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bahama government.</hi> * * *</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>SAMUEL WHITING, <hi rendition="#italic">U. S.
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gideon Welles</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Secretary of the Navy, Washington.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
